# {{app_name}}

A native desktop app for macOS and Linux, built with [GPUI](https://www.gpui.rs/) via
[GPUI Kit](https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit).

## Run it

```bash
cargo run          # or: just run
```

The first build compiles GPUI and takes a few minutes. Rust is pinned in
`rust-toolchain.toml`; rustup installs it. Recipes need [`just`](https://github.com/casey/just)
(`cargo install just`); bundling needs `cargo install cargo-bundle`. On Linux, first install
the system packages listed in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.

```bash
just run-tray     # menu-bar / tray mode
just dry-run      # separate settings file, doesn't take focus
just shot settings dark /tmp/settings.png   # headless screenshot, no window
just ci           # format, lint both feature sets, test, build
just install      # bundle + replace the copy in /Applications (macOS)
```

## Make it yours

1. Replace `src/home.rs`. Its New Item command is also wired up in `src/lib.rs`,
   `src/shell.rs` and `src/palette.rs`.
2. Drop 1024×1024 artwork at `assets/icon-source.png` and run `just icon` (macOS, Pillow).
3. Adjust `[package.metadata.bundle]` in `Cargo.toml` (category, descriptions).

`AGENTS.md` covers the code layout, the checks and upgrading GPUI. `docs/` has GPUI notes.

